.claude/

# Journey-sweep run artifacts. The harness writes journey-sweep-<date>.log/.json on every
# run, so committing them means every sweep dirties the tree with a file whose NAME carries
# a stale date — the first run after midnight would also leave an untracked new file behind.
# They are run dumps, not evidence worth versioning: the sweep is re-runnable on demand and
# its verdict is in the exit code and the JSON. (D-1404.)
journey-sweep-*.log
journey-sweep-*.json

# packaging build artifacts (never commit derived files)
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# npm
node_modules/
*.tgz
npm/.npmrc
